  "body": "`stock_field_cost` reports ms/move and build time, but it asserts only that the run completes. #26 asks for a per-brick update cost law: a stated budget per touched brick, asserted on the heavy lane, so retiring the column engine cannot hide a cost regression.\n\nPart of #26 (retire the column engine). Research and consumer map: https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/issues/26#issuecomment-6754685656\n\nThe step is behaviour-neutral: `stock_engine_agreement` and the goldens stay byte-identical where verdicts are.\n\nDone means: `stock_field_cost` asserts a per-brick update budget (stated in the suite header with its derivation) on every golden program, and fails with the program and move when it is exceeded.\n",
